preConditionHook:
// THE OPENING RANGE MEASURED MOVE -- Brooks's "approximate doubling of the day's
// range" after a breakout of the first bars of the session. A long is closed at
// the opening range's high plus multiple x the range's height, a short at the
// low minus it.
//
// Kept apart from PatternHeightMeasuredMoveTarget, whose reference window is the
// refBars bars before the breakout and moves with it: this window is
// SESSION-ANCHORED and fixed for the whole day once the first openingBars bars
// have printed, so the two project off different bars. Intraday only.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision and identical to OpeningRangeBreakout
// and SessionOpeningRange, which are inlined here rather than referenced: a
// session starts when the wall-clock close date changes -- EL's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)) -- and the running
// extremes plus a bars-into-session counter live in locals reset there. barsIn
// is 1 on the session's first bar.
//
// The target is trusted only once the range is SET (barsIn >= openingBars), the
// same gate OpeningRangeBreakout uses. tolerancePoints takes profit just short
// of the projected level, as the other targets in the bucket do; it is PRICE
// POINTS, not ticks, because MinMove/PriceScale have no engine counterpart --
// 0.25 is one Emini tick and is instrument-specific.
//
// WARM-UP mirrors EL exactly: barsIn, orHigh and orLow hold their initial 0 if
// the first calculated bar falls mid-session, so orLow stays 0.0 until the first
// date change and the short target is unreachable up to that point. Mirrored, not
// corrected.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    orHigh = high[0];
    orLow = low[0];
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    if (barsIn <= (int)openingBars) {
        if (el_gt(high[0], orHigh)) orHigh = high[0];
        if (el_lt(low[0], orLow)) orLow = low[0];
    }
}
orTgtUp = orHigh + multiple * (orHigh - orLow);
orTgtDn = orLow - multiple * (orHigh - orLow);
